From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 22:18:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] Companion shield use: one reactive owner for every task,
 the human reaction, the melee rhythm, GameTests and docs

ShieldGuard is the one owner of a companion's reactive shield, ticked once per bot per server tick from BotTickCoordinator (after the equipment pass, before the mission executor), so following, escorting, mining, gathering, idle and combat bots all block and no two tasks fight over the use hand. It raises the shield through vanilla's use path (MAIN_HAND, then OFF_HAND, as the client does); a main-hand item that would take the use (a bow with ammunition, a loadable crossbow, food, a usable trident, a spear, armour, a throwable, ...: each mirrors the item's own use) makes it change the hotbar first (one tick). It reacts only to what the bot NOTICED:
- a blockable projectile on a hit course, seen in flight or its shot heard with a clear line: at once when its shooter is a creature the bot is tracking (it watched the release), otherwise only after the human reaction time of the shared formula in continuous exposure, so an arrow from a shooter nobody noticed normally lands first;
- a noticed shooter drawing a bow or charging or holding a loaded crossbow aimed at the bot (weapon-neutral): held until the shot lands or the draw stops. The WIP's invented bound (60 ticks of hold, then a 20-tick pause) is gone; a shooter that is the combat target within striking reach is left to the melee rhythm instead, so it cannot freeze a melee exchange;
- a guardian beam locked on the bot (the beam's mob_attack part is blockable) and a late creeper fuse.
A raise is started only when it can be active in time (turn at the human rate into the shield's own arc, block delay); a source with no flight time is raised against only when the bot can face it (a walker steers the head). The hand policy finishes eating and draws unless the hit is lethal; a ranged exchange keeps shooting (its arrow took the offhand). An axe-disabled shield (vanilla item cooldown) is never tried. The offhand content is the equipment rule's (OffhandPolicy.apply: an empty offhand or a totem takes the best shield, anything else stays). While a shield is up the bot neither mines nor attacks (InteractAction.attackEntity now refuses while ANY item is in use, like the client) and moves at vanilla's 0.2 item-use pace; the navigation safety net's rescue stands the guard down.

CombatTask: the melee rhythm follows ShieldRules.meleeStep: the shield comes down only when the weapon is ready AND the target is under the crosshair in reach, and the swing is the next tick's (the client drops the attack click of the tick the use key is released); CombatCore.strikeIfReady lowers a raised shield and swings on the next tick too. The stale comment "a raised shield does not slow a fake player" is gone: controller movement is slowed by PaceRules, and REPOSITION's raw strafe keys now carry the same 0.2 factor, so an approach and a reposition keep moving (slowed) while the guard holds the shield. CreeperDefenseTask raises through the same path and turns at the human rate.

Follower GameTest (h), root cause: it passed 2 of 2 here on the unreviewed WIP, so the old failure did not reproduce; an instrumented run showed its only timing coupling, the invented bound above: the shield was raised at t17, the arrow blocked at t28, the pace window ran t43..t73 and the bound would have dropped the shield at about t84 (60 ticks of hold plus the 7 ticks the arrow was in flight: a margin of 11 ticks; the 40-tick value the same bound had in the old CombatTask would fall inside the window). A dropped shield makes the follower sprint (hostile pressure) and fails the pace check. Product bug (the spec says hold until the shot lands or the draw stops); the fixture premise (a skeleton that keeps aiming) is unchanged, and a check that the follower actually moved on was added.

GameTests (ShieldBlockingGameTests, 11, all with realistic perception ON): a noticed skeleton's arrow blocked with no damage and shield wear; a Piercing bolt from a watched pillager never raised against and hits, while an ordinary bolt on the same course from the same pillager is blocked; a splash potion of harming from a watched witch never raises the shield; an unnoticed shot from behind hits; NEW: an arrow seen in flight from a skeleton not yet noticed lands before the reaction time; a husk's hits blocked between the bot's swings and the husk killed; an axe vindicator disables the shield for the vanilla cooldown with no re-raise attempts and the bot fights on; a primed creeper the bot noticed is faced and blocked for less damage than an unshielded bot takes; a follower blocks an arrow and keeps following at the slowed pace; a bow in the main hand is switched to the sword before the pre-emptive raise; NEW: a guardian beam's bite is blocked and only its magic part hurts. Fixture premises changed with the reaction rule: the arrows of b and i come from a shooter the bot has noticed (a follower standing by its player, so the danger watcher's follow mode keeps it out of a fight), c's potion from a noticed witch, g lights each creeper only after the bot noticed it.

Docs: docs/SHIELD_USE.md (the table from vanilla data, the reaction, the timing, the melee rhythm, the hands), docs/PERCEPTION.md (projectile noticing vs acting on it). Source-contract pins updated faithfully (the guard's call sites, the next-tick swing, the slowed strafe, the safety-net stand-down, the perception call-site count of ShieldGuard).

